DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((sin((7/((x^2))))))^(1/3)");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((sin((cos(((x)^(1/3)))))))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-8, -6, 5} U {-10, -8, -7}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-10, -8, -7} U (-infinity, 12] U (-infinity, 12] U (-infinity, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-10, -8, -7} U {-10, -8, -7} U ((-infinity, 12] U ({-8, -6, 5} U ((-infinity, 12]))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-8, -6, 5})))))");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("({-8, -6, 5} - ((({-10, -8, -7}) U (-infinity, 12] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 12])) U ((-infinity, 12] U {-8, -6, 5} U ((-infinity, 12]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 12]))))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("([2, 7] - [2, 7])");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[2, 7] U [2, 7]");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[2, 7] U {-10, 2, 9, 10}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

For a school art project, Ben brought [`14`] red leaves, [`4`] yellow leaves, [`2`] orange leaves, and [`12`] brown leaves from his backyard. How many leaves did Ben bring for the project in total?

[_____]{32}
[%
14+4+2+12

Add all the leaves together: 14 + 4 = 18, 18 + 2 = 20, 20 + 12 = 32 leaves.
%]
---

Lily collected [`11`] seashells on Monday. On Tuesday, she found [`12`] more seashells at the beach. How many seashells did Lily collect in total over the two days?

[_____]{23}
[%
11+12

Add the seashells from both days: 11 + 12 = 23 seashells.
%]
---

During a board game, Mia started with [`16`] points. She earned [`1`] point on her next turn, then lost [`8`] points on a challenge. Finally, she landed on a special square that gave her [`7`] times the points she had just before landing there, which was [`7`] points. How many points does Mia have at the end?

[_____]{58}
[%
16+1-8+7*7

First, calculate the points from the special square: 7 × 7 = 49 points. Then, calculate the running total: Start with 16, add 1 (16 + 1 = 17), subtract 8 (17 - 8 = 9). Finally, add the points from the special square: 9 + 49 = 58 points.
%]
---

A class is making friendship bracelets. They have [`11`] blue beads, [`2`] green beads, and [`13`] red beads. They decide to use [`9`] beads to make a sample bracelet, and then share the remaining beads equally among [`13`] students to finish their projects. How many beads will be left for the class to share after making the sample? (Give the answer as a decimal).

[_____]{25.3076923077}
[%
11+2+13-9/13

First, calculate the total beads: 11 + 2 + 13 = 26 beads. Next, calculate how many beads are used for the sample bracelet: 9 beads. Then, find the beads remaining: 26 - 9 = 17 beads. Finally, to find how many beads are left for the class to share (which is the result of the original expression), we perform the operations in order: 11 + 2 = 13, 13 + 13 = 26, 26 - (9 ÷ 13). Calculate 9 ÷ 13 ≈ 0.6923076923. Subtract this from 26: 26 - 0.6923076923 ≈ 25.3076923077 beads.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 2 \leq x \leq 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, 2, 9, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -8, -7\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 12\}`]
- [`C = \{-8, -6, 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup B \cup B \cup B \cap ((A \cup A \cup (B \cup (C \cup (B))) \cap (C))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`C - (((A) \cup B \cap B) \cup (B \cup C \cup (B) \cap B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, -5, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, -6, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, -5, 2>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-7, -5, 2>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, -5, 2>") . Compute("<-4, -6, -8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, -5, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, -5, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, -6, -8>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, -7, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, -1, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, -9, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, -1, 8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -1, 8>") x Compute("<-8, -7, -1>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -1, 8>") . Compute("<9, -9, 2>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -9, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -9, 2>") . Compute("<-8, -7, -1>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---
END_PGML
